# Number display

API/DB keep raw numbers. UI formats with `formatNumber` only.

```ts
const { formatNumber } = useNumberFormat()

formatNumber(1234567)        // vi: 1.234.567 · en: 1,234,567
formatNumber(1234.5)         // keeps 1 decimal
formatNumber(1234.567)       // keeps 3 decimals
formatNumber(1234.5, { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })
```

Helpers: `frontend/composables/useNumberFormat.ts`, `frontend/utils/number.ts`.

## Forbidden

- `toLocaleString` / `toFixed` / hard-coded `,` `.` separators in pages
- Formatting numbers in the API for UI

Locale follows i18n: `vi` → `vi-VN`, `en` → `en-US`. Null/NaN → `''`.  
Default fraction digits follow the input (trailing zeros dropped by JS are fine).
